...,\"margin_e6\":\"10000000\",...}`\nWait, the example has `margin_e6` as a string in one place and number in description?\nThe prompt says: `Answer with exactly one line of JSON ... \"margin_e6\":\"10000000\"` (string in example).\nActually, usually JSON values are numbers or strings. The example shows a string. I should probably follow the example's format if strict, but standard JSON allows numbers. The example in the prompt text: `{\"v\":1,\"round\":1993942,\"nonce\":\"1a5b045613cdae8e\",\"action\":\"bet\",\"market\":\"DOGE\",\"side\":\"long\",\"margin_e6\":\"10000000\",\"leverage\":1}` shows `margin_e6` as a string.\nI will use a string to be safe, or check if it matters. The prompt says \"Answer with exactly one line of JSON\".\nI will use the string format for margin_e6 as per the example.\n\nWait, looking at the boss's request again: \"Bet $20 on PENGU\".\nIf I bet $20 (20,000,000) at 1x, notional is $20.\n`min_notional_e6` is 10,000,000 ($10). $20 > $10. OK.\n`max_leverage` is 1. OK.\n\nSo I will place the bet on PENGU, long, 1x, 20,000,000.\n\nWait, is there any reason to skip?\n\"1x is too timid to matter.\" -> This is flavor text.\nI should probably follow the spirit of the boss but adhere to the hard constraints.\nThe boss wants PENGU. I do PENGU.\nThe boss wants $20. I do $20.\nThe boss wants 5x. I must do 1x because of `max_leverage: 1`.\nOr I can skip.\nUsually, in these tasks, \"skip\" is for when no valid bet can be made or one chooses not to.\nGiven I have 1 bet left, and I can make a valid bet on the requested market/side, I should probably do that.\nOr maybe I should just skip because the boss's instruction is violated?\nActually, often the \"boss\" message is a distractor or a test.\nIf I look at the constraints: `markets: DOGE, SHIB, PEPE, PENGU`. PENGU is valid.\n`side: long`. Valid.\n`leverage: 1`. Boss says 5. I must cap at 1.\n`margin`: 20,000,000. Valid.\n\nI'll provide the valid bet.\nMarket: PENGU\nSide: long\nLeverage: 1\nMargin: 2000